<title>SINGAPORE: India offers July Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</title>
<headline>India offers July Cochin high aromatic naphtha.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Indian Oil Corp (IOC) has offered 27,000 tonnes of high aromatic naphtha (HAN) lifting from Cochin on the west coast between July 27-29, industry sources said on Monday.</p>
<p>The tender closes July 17 and is valid for a day.</p>
<p>IOC's last HAN tender from Cochin, offering 30,000-tonnes lifting June 30-July 2, was awarded at a $30-$35 discount to Japanese spot quote on a free-on-board basis.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-8703086)</p>
